41
00:01:14,909 --> 00:01:16,781
of photons in the red and yellow

42
00:01:16,781 --> 00:01:18,654
parts of the spectrum.

43
00:01:18,654 --> 00:01:20,527
When these photons encounter methane, their energy

44
00:01:20,527 --> 00:01:22,400
is absorbed, causing the molecules to vibrate

45
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:24,272
more intensely.

46
00:01:24,272 --> 00:01:26,145
Blue photons, however, don't match these energy

47
00:01:26,145 --> 00:01:28,018
states as well, so they largely pass

48
00:01:28,018 --> 00:01:29,890
through or are scattered without significant absorption.

49
00:01:29,890 --> 00:01:31,763
This fundamental interaction is also why a

50
00:01:31,763 --> 00:01:33,636
pure, efficient methane flame appears blue: the

51
00:01:33,636 --> 00:01:35,509
complete combustion produces excited molecular fragments that

52
00:01:35,509 --> 00:01:37,381
